### Saga Demo — REST Client test scenarios
### Compatible with IntelliJ HTTP Client and VS Code REST Client.
### Each "###" header is a separate runnable request.

@order = http://localhost:8081
@inventory = http://localhost:8083
@ui = http://localhost:8080

@customer1 = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@customer2 = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002

@notebook   = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@keyboard   = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@mouse      = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@monitor    = 44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444
@gpu        = 55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555
@mug        = 66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666
@hoodie     = 77777777-7777-7777-7777-777777777777


### 1. List products (see current stock — REST view)
GET {{inventory}}/api/products
Accept: application/json


### 2. Get current stock engine mode
GET {{inventory}}/admin/stock-engine
Accept: application/json


### 3. Happy path — 2 notebooks at 100 each (total 200, well under fail threshold)
# @name happyOrder
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: scen-happy-001

{
  "customerId": "{{customer1}}",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{notebook}}", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 100.00 }
  ]
}


### 4. Read back the order — saga should reach COMPLETED within ~3s
GET {{order}}/api/orders/{{happyOrder.response.body.orderId}}
Accept: application/json


### 5. Idempotency replay — SAME key as request 3 → same orderId, no new saga
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: scen-happy-001

{
  "customerId": "{{customer1}}",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{notebook}}", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 100.00 }
  ]
}


### 6. Compensating path — total = 6000 > 5000 fail-above threshold
# @name failingOrder
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: scen-paymentfail-001

{
  "customerId": "{{customer2}}",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{monitor}}", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 3000.00 }
  ]
}


### 7. Verify compensating ran: saga FAILED, order CANCELLED, monitor stock back to 5
GET {{order}}/api/orders/{{failingOrder.response.body.orderId}}
Accept: application/json


### 8. Insufficient stock — request 11 GPUs (only 10 in stock)
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: scen-oversell-001

{
  "customerId": "{{customer1}}",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{gpu}}", "quantity": 11, "unitPrice": 50.00 }
  ]
}


### 9. Unknown product — should fail at inventory engine with UnknownProduct
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: scen-unknown-001

{
  "customerId": "{{customer1}}",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 10.00 }
  ]
}


### 10. Multi-item order — happy
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: scen-multi-001

{
  "customerId": "{{customer1}}",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{mug}}", "quantity": 3, "unitPrice": 5.00 },
    { "productId": "{{keyboard}}", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 150.00 }
  ]
}


### 11. List all orders
GET {{order}}/api/orders
Accept: application/json


### 12. Admin — flip to DATABASE engine (reconciles Redis -> Postgres first)
POST {{inventory}}/admin/stock-engine/DATABASE


### 13. Place an order while DATABASE mode is active (pessimistic-lock path)
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: scen-db-mode-001

{
  "customerId": "{{customer1}}",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{mug}}", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 5.00 }
  ]
}


### 14. Admin — flip back to REDIS (warms Redis from Postgres first)
POST {{inventory}}/admin/stock-engine/REDIS


### 15. Verify mode is REDIS again
GET {{inventory}}/admin/stock-engine


### 16. Verify product counts after all scenarios
GET {{inventory}}/api/products
Accept: application/json
